    "bio": "Z-Trip (born Zach Sciacca) is a Phoenix, Arizona native. He was known early in his career for performing with the Bombshelter DJs (DJ Emile, DJ Radar, and DJ Z-Trip). He became widely known when his collaboration with DJ P, Uneasy Listening, Volume 1, was released in 2001. Only 2000 copies were made, but the album was soon distributed over the Internet in MP3 format. Z-Trip contributed several pieces of work to EA Games' release Skate. Z-Trip is one of the biggest DJs of our time doing over 100 shows a year, every year."
